findings.body:
Right after `Action.SelectLightTheme`, the test now reads the **dark** theme button's value and expects it to be `"1"`. Once Light is selected, dark is deselected (`"0"`), so this assertion fails every time. If the selector were broken instead, the test would be checking the wrong control.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="46-55"}

The PR description says this test was being *aligned* with the new TestRail case's steps. Changing the identifier doesn't fit that, and this test is in both the Accessibility and TAESmoke plans.

